  "Question": "For the entire graph of an upward-opening quadratic function to lie above the \\(x\\)-axis, what must be true of the discriminant?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "It equals 0",
    "B": "It is less than 0",
    "C": "It is greater than 0",
    "D": "It can be any real number"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The entire graph lies above the axis only when there are no intersection points, so the discriminant is less than 0. When it equals 0, the graph touches the \\(x\\)-axis.",
